All 13 tests pass — every endpoint, every auth check, every edge case. Here's a summary of what was built:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now guards on `None` header, then `VALID_API_KEYS` lookup, raising 401 with a distinct message for each failure mode. Returns the username on success for downstream use.

**`app/main.py`** — six changes:

| Endpoint | What changed |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` query params + `page`/`page_size` pagination. Filters compose; unfiltered returns all. |
| `POST /tasks` | Auth-protected via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` against the projects list (404 if missing). Auto-generates sequential IDs from `itertools.count`. Returns 201. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | Auth-protected. `TaskUpdate.model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` applies only supplied fields. Returns 404 if the task id doesn't exist. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | Auth-protected. Removes from the in-memory list. Returns 204 + 404. |

The existing `GET /projects` and `GET /tasks/{task_id}` endpoints are unchanged.
